# Paths the document-deslop skill never runs on.
#
# One repo-relative path, directory, or glob per line; a directory covers its
# whole subtree; `**` matches any number of directories, including
# none; `#` opens a comment line. Every entry carries a comment
# saying why. Unlike .deslopped, an entry here records no sha: exemption is
# permanent and does not lapse when the file changes.

# The catalog the skill reads to do its job. Every `**Before** "..."` in it is
# a deliberate specimen of a tic, so an agent applying the standard to this
# file would destroy the examples that define it.
standards/prose/slop-tics.md

# Indexes. Each entry restates the frontmatter `description` of the file it
# links, and okf-lint fails the commit when the two drift. The description is
# the target file's to change, so an index is never rewritten on its own.
**/index.md
